_tbv":0.0,"_gate_mult_vs_hist":-0.6916311856398818,"_gp_mult_vs_hist":true,"_score_mult_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.03466117439400374,"_gp_fcf_yield":false,"_score_fcf_yield":12.0,"_gate_int_coverage":49.82513661202186,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":100.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-0.7886730835338605,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":100.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.09533273395479425,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":67.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.157271921079419,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":69.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.1302802765530031,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.21540134820978069,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.4128104055362951,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.19944062348177047,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":99.8,"_gate_pool_share":0.16359537472539443,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.2777168484798116,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.31246833350776404,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.021325636699978622,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":28.7,"_gate_fund_growth":0.2858924963071109,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.015184374486196034,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":28.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.007854375912587197,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":59.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03423423423423423,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":42.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00259,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"DexCom, Inc., a medical device company, focuses on the design, development, and commercialization of continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) systems for the management of diabetes and metabolic health in the United States and internationally. The company offers Dexcom G7 and G7 15 Day, an integrated continuous glucose monitoring system; Dexcom G6, a CGM system; Dexcom ONE+ to replace fingerstick blood glucose testing for diabetes treatment decisions; Stelo, a biosensor designed for adults with prediabetes and Type 2 diabetes who do not use insulin; Dexcom Share, a remote monitoring system; and Dexcom Follow application. It markets its products directly to endocrinologists, physicians, and diabetes educators. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jacob Steven Leach | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $424K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 34%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $98K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["DexCom, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $31.1B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +28% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +5.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 32% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 22-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 64% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.72\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 50\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 44% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4443724828448313},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 29% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 20% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is DexCom (DXCM) Reasonably Priced After Raised Guidance And G7 Progress?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-dxcm/dexcom/news/is-dexcom-dxcm-reasonably-priced-after-raised-guidance-and-g","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526601.48,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"DexCom (DXCM) Could Be 32% Undervalued Following Health Canada G7 Pregnancy Clearance","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/dexcom-dxcm-could-32-undervalued-081533028.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471333.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Pregnancy Device Approval At DexCom (DXCM) Has Changed Its Investment Story","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/pregnancy-device-approval-dexcom-dxcm-071133723.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794467493.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"Pregnancy Device Approval Could Be A Big Deal For DexCom (DXCM)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-dxcm/dexcom/news/pregnancy-device-approval-could-be-a-big-deal-for-dexcom-dxc","date":"2026-11-11","ti